@*
    The gate's verdict.

    A blocked status is rendered as a DECISION, not as an error. The API returns 200 for
    blocked_pending_approval because it is a successful assessment whose answer is "no" — it
    carries reasons, citations and audit ids. Styling it like a failure would invite a reviewer
    to treat a policy outcome as a transport problem and retry it, which is exactly the
    confusion the status-code choice was made to avoid.

    So blocked states get their own "gated" treatment, distinct from both success and error.
*@

<span class="oc-badge oc-badge--action-@Status.Wire()" data-action-status="@Status.Wire()">
    <span class="oc-badge__label">Action</span>
    <span class="oc-badge__value">@Status.Label()</span>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The gate's verdict on the requested action.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public ActionStatusDto Status { get; set; }
}
